{"parentUuid":"da53b9b0-d084-4e91-a2af-dd88816888ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHHhyua3HydaABEs8owLtQ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Painless SAT framework parallel clause sharing Sharer architecture\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallel Clause Sharing Strategy Based on Graph Structure of SAT Problem\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol305-sat2024/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01540785v1/document\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/391418351_D-Painless_A_Framework_for_Distributed_Portfolio_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: a Framework for Parallel SAT Solving. - LRDE\",\"url\":\"https://www.lrde.epita.fr/dload/papers/le-frioux.17.sat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318986849_PaInleSS_A_Framework_for_Parallel_SAT_Solving\"},{\"title\":\"D-Painless: A Framework for Distributed Portfolio SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-90653-4_3\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] PaInleSS: A Framework for Parallel SAT Solving | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/PaInleSS:-A-Framework-for-Parallel-SAT-Solving-Frioux-Baarir/8d6870ab6c3abbb7b952fde8ffb2e57da8bf2747\"},{\"title\":\"Scalable Proof Producing Multi-Threaded SAT Solving with ...\",\"url\":\"https://cca.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/papers/FleuryBiere-ARXIV22.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lip6/painless: A framework to ease parallelization of sequential SAT solvers\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lip6/painless\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the Painless SAT framework and its parallel clause sharing architecture:\n\n## Painless Framework Overview\n\nPainless is a flexible framework for parallel and distributed SAT solving that integrates multiple state-of-the-art SAT solvers and preprocessing techniques. The PaInLeSS framework offers a modular architecture to \"painlessly\" develop and explore parallel SAT solvers.\n\n## Sharer Architecture\n\nThe framework employs a worker-sharer architecture for clause sharing. It adopts worker-sharer architecture where workers generate learnt clauses through search, with only learnt clauses with LBD values of either 1 or 2 submitted to the buffer, and the sharer broadcasts these clauses in the buffer to other workers up to 1500 literal lengths per sharing cycle.\n\nThe SharingStrategy facilitates clause sharing among its producers and consumers, with the Sharer representing the thread that executes the chosen SharingStrategy.\n\n## Clause Sharing Strategies\n\nThe framework offers parallelization via portfolios, clause sharing, and search space partitioning. ParKissat-RS and PRS adopted the painless framework and used LBD as the criteria to determine the clauses to be shared.\n\n## Recent Extensions\n\nA revised structure establishes a coherent hierarchy and interaction schema for both locally parallel and distributed SAT solvers, enabling more robust clause sharing mechanisms.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5e3898b7-24a4-4449-b679-79c405df2ef1","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:44.513Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"da53b9b0-d084-4e91-a2af-dd88816888ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"98bd61a0-eddb-4148-aadb-8463c11de2c1","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WbfL8oqmssst3k4cteikq","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT multi worker clause sharing internal architecture shared_clauses\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Clause Sharing Strategy Based on Graph Structure of SAT Problem\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol305-sat2024/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17/LIPIcs.SAT.2024.17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Control-Based Clause Sharing in Parallel SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/978-3-642-21434-9_10.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Seeding CP-SAT solver\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/lPb1FzhTMt0\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about OR-Tools CP-SAT multi-worker clause sharing:\n\n## Clause Sharing in CP-SAT Multi-Worker Architecture\n\nCP-SAT is a portfolio-solver that uses different techniques to solve the problem, with some information exchange between different workers, but does not split the solution space into different parts.\n\n### Clause Sharing Mechanisms\n\nCP-SAT concurrently executes diverse algorithms and strategies, with these elements operating largely independently while engaging in information exchange, sharing progress when better solutions emerge or tighter bounds become available.\n\nThe system includes clause sharing between workers, which is verified when checking LRAT proofs for UNSAT problems.\n\n### Configuration Parameters\n\nThere is a parameter `share_glue_clauses_dtime` with a default value of 1.0, related to sharing clauses. The search results also reference a `share_binary_clause` parameter that can be configured in multi-worker scenarios.\n\n### Performance Considerations\n\nThe multi-worker approach leverages information sharing where workers can share solutions and bounds with the rest of the portfolio, boosting overall performance.\n\nFor more detailed information about the internal architecture and the `shared_clauses` implementation specifics, you may need to consult the OR-Tools source code directly, particularly the `sat_parameters.proto` and related solver implementation files.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"96011f9a-6c56-4831-9556-f7c4afb44301","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:45.847Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"98bd61a0-eddb-4148-aadb-8463c11de2c1","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"46a50d57-e583-4c28-bf2b-59bb71e6a8b4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UcYFPyCmu8gRbArxsNRfnJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Mallob distributed SAT solver clause sharing scaling 1000 cores\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing\",\"url\":\"https://dominikschreiber.de/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2205.06590] Scalable SAT Solving in the Cloud\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2205.06590\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/383383402_MallobSat_Scalable_SAT_Solving_by_Clause_Sharing\"},{\"title\":\"Unsatisfiability Proofs for Distributed Clause-Sharing SAT Solvers | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-30823-9_18\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing | Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/view/15827\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing - SAtRes\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2024-jair-mallobsat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"MallobSat: : Scalable SAT Solving by Clause Sharing: Journal of Artificial Intelligence Research: Vol 80, No null\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1613/jair.1.15827\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - domschrei/mallob: Malleable Load Balancer. Massively Parallel Logic Backend. Award-winning SAT solving for the cloud.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/domschrei/mallob\"},{\"title\":\"Producing Proofs of Unsatisfiability with Distributed Clause-Sharing SAT Solvers | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-025-09725-w\"},{\"title\":\"From Scalable SAT to MaxSAT: Massively Parallel Solution Improving Search\",\"url\":\"https://satres.kikit.kit.edu/papers/2025-socs-distributed-maxsat.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about Mallob, distributed SAT solver clause sharing, and its scaling to 1000 cores:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nMallob is a distributed platform for automated reasoning in modern large-scale HPC and cloud environments that primarily solves instances of propositional satisfiability (SAT).\n\n### Clause Sharing Approach\n\nMallobSat presents a communication-efficient approach to clause sharing, careful buffering and filtering of produced clauses, and effective orchestration of state-of-the-art solver backends. The clause sharing results in effective parallelization even if all threads execute identical solver programs that only differ based on which clauses they import at which times.\n\n### Scaling Performance\n\nMallobSat significantly outperforms an updated HordeSat, doubling its mean speedup. More importantly, MallobSat at 3072 cores solves several instances that presumably have never been solved before, demonstrating its capability to scale well beyond 1000 cores.\n\nFor proof production at massive scale, empirical evaluation with over 1500 solver threads shows that the distributed approach allows proof composition and checking within around 3× its own solving time.\n\n### Recognition\n\nMallob and its tightly integrated distributed general-purpose SAT solving engine, MallobSat, received five gold medals in the International SAT Competition's Cloud Track in a row.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"edf3056d-c29e-4f2a-a9a8-2bb02f7702d4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:46.318Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"46a50d57-e583-4c28-bf2b-59bb71e6a8b4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"0f6d7ac2-0366-4b7e-84d0-a8f9d206f97b","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014UndQn6ipbhrKdRLWKVzdx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT export learned clauses hook patch github issue\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Sat: Python 3.7.2, ortools 7.0 wrong optimization result · Issue #1162 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1162\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver returning non-optimal solutions with status \\\"OPTIMAL\\\" · Issue #3639 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3639\"},{\"title\":\"google/or-tools Cp Sat Questions · Discussions\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/categories/cp-sat-questions\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and learned clauses, though the results don't show a specific GitHub issue dedicated solely to \"export learned clauses hook patch.\"\n\nHere's what I found:\n\nThe OR-Tools CP-SAT solver has parameters related to exporting shared clauses, with \"the amount of dtime between each export of shared glue clauses\" controlled by a parameter, and there is discussion of checking inferred clauses as they are learned.\n\nCP-SAT is described as a next-gen Constraint Programming solver with clause learning, built on top of an efficient SAT/max-SAT solver.\n\nThe solver keeps learned clauses during search restarts, which allows it to recover from bad decisions and lead to smaller search trees by learning from past mistakes.\n\nThe search results show various GitHub issues related to CP-SAT but don't display a specific issue titled \"export learned clauses hook patch.\" The results indicate that clause management and export functionality exists within the CP-SAT parameters (as seen in the sat_parameters.proto file), but a more specific GitHub issue number or direct link to the patch you're looking for wasn't returned in these results.\n\nIf you're looking for a specific GitHub issue number or pull request, you might want to search directly on GitHub's issue tracker or provide more specific details about the issue.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8e9322de-01c5-4263-86bc-cb932018a833","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:05:46.336Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0f6d7ac2-0366-4b7e-84d0-a8f9d206f97b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
