{"parentUuid":"a56a2be3-b321-4b00-b062-fec039888251","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8gURdy5ZrciSL3wucdcHZ","type":"tool_result","content":"# Painless SAT Solver Framework Analysis\n\n## Integrated Solvers\n\nPainless wraps eight established SAT solvers: \"Kissat (v4.0.2), CaDiCaL (v1.9.1), MapleCOMSPS, Glucose, MiniSat, Lingeling, YalSAT,\" plus Kissat variants (MAB and INC).\n\n## Adding New Solvers\n\nThe documentation mentions a \"Solver interface and implementations\" component in `src/solvers/`, but the provided content doesn't detail the integration process. You'd need to consult the development documentation or source code directly.\n\n## Sharer Interface\n\nThe framework includes \"Learnt clause sharing management and strategies\" in `src/sharing/`, but specifics about the Sharer interface aren't explained in this excerpt.\n\n## Licensing\n\nThe repository includes a LICENSE file, though its specific terms aren't detailed in the excerpt. The framework integrates open-source solvers with their respective licenses.\n\n## Real-World Performance Gains\n\nThe content doesn't provide comparative benchmarks demonstrating performance improvements from clause sharing versus non-sharing portfolios. The references section cites academic papers that might contain this analysis.\n\n**For complete details on solver integration, the Sharer interface, and performance metrics, consult the full documentation or referenced academic papers.**"}]},"uuid":"e2a43d26-4bd7-4bbe-9a8e-6d88afe12fa9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:00.725Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a56a2be3-b321-4b00-b062-fec039888251","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
