{"parentUuid":"37cf535b-1723-40e2-9a9c-e1d4f15234ac","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LUAWEZg9gNArF1pn4q8mZV","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" \"SharedClausesManager\" OR \"synchronization_layer\" cp_solver.cc source\"\n\nNo links found.\n\nThe search returned no results. This suggests that the specific combination of these terms—particularly \"SharedClausesManager\" and \"synchronization_layer\" in relation to the \"cp_solver.cc\" source file in OR-Tools—may not be widely indexed or publicly documented, or the exact terminology might differ from what's available online.\n\nThese appear to be internal implementation details from the Google OR-Tools library (an operations research optimization toolkit). If you're looking for information about these specific components, you might want to:\n\n1. Check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly for the source code\n2. Consult the official OR-Tools documentation\n3. Look at the source code comments or commit history for context about these components\n\nIs there something specific about OR-Tools or constraint programming optimization you'd like to know more about?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"57342d4b-85d1-46b3-992c-653d2da4fe33","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:15.329Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"37cf535b-1723-40e2-9a9c-e1d4f15234ac","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"eb5a8c89-48b9-457c-93d0-51b06130defa","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01877gbjJzt2SbiHYJGLncVD","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT shared_tree_workers shared bounds manager source code\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for cpmpy.solvers.ortools\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"✨ Recipes for Google OR-Tools | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT's shared tree workers and bounds manager:\n\n## Key Findings\n\nShared tree workers explore a shared search tree, where workers communicate objective bounds and simple decision nogoods relating to the shared prefix of the tree, and avoid exploring the same subtrees as one another.\n\nThere is a parameter `shared_tree_num_workers` (option 235) which is set on shared subtree workers.\n\nThe parameter `shared_tree_max_nodes_per_worker` (option 238, default 10000) controls the maximum nodes per worker.\n\nThe source code reference for these parameters can be found in the OR-Tools GitHub repository at the sat_parameters.proto file, which defines the configuration options for the CP-SAT solver including the shared tree worker settings.\n\nFor accessing the actual source code implementation of the shared bounds manager and tree workers, you would need to look in the Google OR-Tools GitHub repository (https://github.com/google/or-tools) in the `ortools/sat/` directory, which contains the C++ implementation of these components, though the search results did not return direct links to the specific implementation files.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"742a5d40-c4ec-41ef-b274-6eb33b3d2383","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:18.047Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eb5a8c89-48b9-457c-93d0-51b06130defa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"cbc71acd-c9af-45b0-8c35-6ed7655cf8ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XFreb1czuRaw4XvZwZC9eq","type":"tool_result","content":"# Mallob Solver Backends and Architecture\n\nBased on the GitHub repository content provided, I can address some of your questions:\n\n## Supported Solver Backends\n\nThe documentation mentions several SAT solver backends integrated into Mallob:\n- **Kissat** (referenced as `-satsolver=k`)\n- **Lingeling** (MIT-licensed)\n- **YalSAT** (MIT-licensed)\n- **CaDiCaL** (MIT-licensed)\n- **Glucose** (optional, non-free license)\n\nHowever, the content does **not** specify support for OR-Tools CP-SAT or constraint programming solvers. Mallob appears focused specifically on propositional satisfiability (SAT) solving rather than general constraint programming.\n\n## Limitations of Available Information\n\nThe repository documentation provided does not contain details about:\n- The specific inter-process communication architecture for clause sharing (whether MPI-based, shared memory, or hybrid)\n- Clause filtering mechanisms or strategies\n- Architectural diagrams or technical specifications\n\n## Where to Find Details\n\nThe README directs users to consult `docs/setup.md`, `docs/execute.md`, and `docs/develop.md` for comprehensive technical information. These files likely contain the architectural details you're seeking but aren't included in the provided excerpt."}]},"uuid":"12c1766b-9be6-4bb8-9f1f-e12ad75bfcb9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:18.971Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cbc71acd-c9af-45b0-8c35-6ed7655cf8ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"52cf063e-f34f-4047-aaa7-593da35c13da","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011NEW4UJmXauGLR4gRkL7hV","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Nondeterminism Issue Analysis\n\nBased on the GitHub issue content provided, I cannot find specific statements from Laurent Perron or other OR-Tools maintainers regarding CP-SAT's parallel determinism, clause sharing between workers, or how `share_glue_clauses` operates internally.\n\nThe issue page shows:\n- A bug report filed by Mapiarz on December 10, 2022\n- The problem: CP-SAT produces different solutions across runs in versions 9.4-9.5, despite setting `num_search_workers` to 1\n- Assignment to lperron (Laurent Perron)\n- Milestone: v9.6\n\nHowever, **no responses, comments, or technical explanations from maintainers are visible** in the provided content. To find discussions about parallel determinism and clause-sharing mechanisms, you would need to access the full issue thread, pull requests, or the OR-Tools documentation directly."}]},"uuid":"982b87a5-88ea-479a-ae98-d88109793874","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:19.653Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52cf063e-f34f-4047-aaa7-593da35c13da","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
