tion. The search results include documentation about SharedResponseManager, which manages the global best response kept by the solver and is responsible for logging the progress of solutions and bounds as they are found.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific information about the `synchronization_function` or `SharedClausesManager` components you're looking for. These appear to be more specialized or internal implementation details of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\n\nTo find more detailed information about these specific C++ implementation details, you might want to:\n\n1. Check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly for the source code\n2. Look at the OR-Tools C++ API reference documentation\n3. Search the OR-Tools discussion groups for threads about these specific components\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about any of these components, or do you need help with a particular aspect of the CP-SAT solver implementation?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dcf2fff0-e08a-4815-a5e4-aaf8b17d97b8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:28.059Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"498f2079-5bd1-4fbf-af02-15116da39218","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3e0a249a-0209-4aee-9291-54370e38d45a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01THiuouYocor5S7RHbJHJyL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT cross process shared memory clause sharing python multiprocessing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"multiprocessing.shared_memory — Shared memory for direct access across processes\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/multiprocessing.shared_memory.html\"},{\"title\":\"multiprocessing — Process-based parallelism\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/multiprocessing.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: not all threads are used, why? · Issue #2399 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2399\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Tinker-Twins/Python-Shared-Memory: Shared Memory Block Between Multiple Python Processes · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Tinker-Twins/Python-Shared-Memory\"},{\"title\":\"Python Shared Memory in Multiprocessing – Mingze Gao\",\"url\":\"https://mingze-gao.com/posts/python-shared-memory-in-multiprocessing/\"},{\"title\":\"multiprocessing — Process-based parallelism — Python 3.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3.9/library/multiprocessing.html\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use SharedMemory in Python - Super Fast Python\",\"url\":\"https://superfastpython.com/multiprocessing-sharedmemory/\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use Python Multiprocessing for Better Performance - StrataScratch\",\"url\":\"https://www.stratascratch.com/blog/how-to-use-python-multiprocessing\"},{\"title\":\"multiprocessing — Process-based parallelism — Python 3.8.20 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://docs.python.org/3.8/library/multiprocessing.html\"},{\"title\":\"Multiprocessing in Python | Set 2 (Communication between processes) - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python/multiprocessing-python-set-2/\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query. The results primarily cover:\n\n1. **Python Shared Memory** - Information about the multiprocessing.shared_memory module, which provides a class for the allocation and management of shared memory to be accessed by one or more processes.\n\n2. **Multiprocessing in Python** - Data can be stored in a shared memory map using Value or Array objects to share data between processes.\n\n3. **OR-Tools CP-SAT Threading** - A GitHub issue discussing thread usage in OR-Tools CP-SAT solver where users reported the solver not utilizing all available threads despite setting num_search_workers.\n\n4. **Shared Memory Implementation** - SharedMemory allows processes to read and write from the same memory, which is faster and more efficient than sharing data via message passing.\n\nThe search results show information about Python's native multiprocessing shared memory capabilities, but there doesn't appear to be specific documentation combining OR-Tools CP-SAT with cross-process shared memory clause sharing in the results. If you're looking for specific documentation on how to share clauses or solver state between OR-Tools CP-SAT instances using Python multiprocessing, you may need to consult the OR-Tools GitHub repository or documentation directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"bcc50ecb-3334-40d6-82a5-82ae4273887d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:29.740Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3e0a249a-0209-4aee-9291-54370e38d45a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
