{"parentUuid":"72b89234-e71e-4d7d-899f-025edf66a2d6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"56e72661-9c70-4718-ac89-40d9fd2179ff","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GQWhM9RQnmT6pFvt7apsLd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools issue feature request export learned clauses between processes Laurent Perron\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Cut generators in CPModelProto · Issue #912 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/912\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron help\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/Jhw6c8CUgF8\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://research.google/people/105821/\"},{\"title\":\"Operations Research and Algorithms at Google Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://aixia2015.unife.it/wp-content/uploads/slides/invited/Perron-OR_at_Google.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent Perron\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=umrglaIAAAAJ&hl=en\"},{\"title\":\"lperron (Laurent Perron) · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lperron\"},{\"title\":\"Is there some articles or other materials about the detail of the tools implementation？ · Issue #920 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/920\"},{\"title\":\"What happened to .NET ConstraintSolver CpModelLoader.IntegerExpressionByName · Issue #905 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/905\"},{\"title\":\"Laurent PERRON | Tech Lead Operations Research | PhD Computer Science | Google Inc., Mountain View | Google | Research Department | Research profile\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Laurent-Perron-2\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools and Laurent Perron's work on clause learning and sharing between processes.\n\nLaurent Perron is working on Operations Research, and his contributions are visible in the OR-Tools package. \n\nRegarding the specific feature of exporting learned clauses between processes, research on parallelizing the state-of-the-art CP-SAT solver investigates the effectiveness of splitting the search space, noting that one key barrier is that generated sub-problems are not independent. The contributions to mitigate this issue include job reassignment and trail sharing, where workers can share some of the state from their local trail when a job is reassigned to a new worker if the clause database appears ill-suited to the region of the search-space.\n\nThese approaches complement standard portfolio and clause-sharing approaches, improving CP-SAT's performance on MiniZinc challenge benchmarks.\n\nThe search results indicate that clause sharing between workers/processes is an established technique being used to improve parallel performance in OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver, though the specific GitHub issue about this feature request was not directly located in these results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"9b1b2ddf-eafd-4927-bfe4-7aa6aa239a88","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:06:43.212Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"72b89234-e71e-4d7d-899f-025edf66a2d6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
