{"parentUuid":"ffa254e5-e167-4dcf-b2b2-93a5e22ef640","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b52db07-c10e-437b-a08d-e086ce9c32e9","agentId":"a38ef37448d2d0a8d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012enPhyoei3sHVRPkUBpyjJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"parallelizing CP-SAT MiniZinc challenge \"trail sharing\" \"job reassignment\" paper 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parallelising Lazy Clause Generation with Trail Sharing | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-95973-8_13\"},{\"title\":\"Google Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://scholar.google.com/scholar?q=Parallelising+Lazy+Clause+Generation+with+Trail+Sharing.\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Results\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/results/\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge 2024 Rules\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/rules/\"},{\"title\":\"description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/2024/description_or-tools_cp-sat.txt\"},{\"title\":\"MiniZinc - Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.minizinc.org/challenge/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) SUNNY-CP and the MiniZinc challenge\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/317958574_SUNNY-CP_and_the_MiniZinc_challenge\"},{\"title\":\"3.5. Solving Technologies and Solver Backends — The MiniZinc Handbook 2.9.7\",\"url\":\"https://docs.minizinc.dev/en/stable/solvers.html\"},{\"title\":\"[1706.08627] SUNNY-CP and the MiniZinc Challenge\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.08627\"},{\"title\":\"ViolationLS: Constraint-Based Local Search in CP-SAT | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-60597-0_16\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found a paper on this topic:\n\nThe paper discusses how jobs (sub-trees) are reassigned to new workers if the clause database of the currently assigned worker appears ill-suited to the region of the search-space, and when doing so workers can share some of the state from their local trail.\n\nThese approaches of job reassignment and trail sharing complement standard portfolio and clause-sharing approaches, improving CP-SAT's performance on MiniZinc challenge benchmarks with a moderate number of worker threads.\n\nA trail prefix can be viewed as a lossy compressed representation of much of the relevant information a worker has learnt about a job, and this information can be exploited by the next worker assigned the same subtree to avoid some redundant work.\n\nThe paper titled \"Parallelising Lazy Clause Generation with Trail Sharing\" appears to be published through Springer Nature (accessible at link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-95973-8_13) and discusses parallelization techniques for CP-SAT solvers in the context of the MiniZinc challenge, incorporating the \"trail sharing\" and \"job reassignment\" concepts you mentioned.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"99a6e848-03b3-4a72-978e-e35cf1c96ce9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:07:17.586Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ffa254e5-e167-4dcf-b2b2-93a5e22ef640","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
